A Node is an individual unit of work in a LangGraph workflow. Each node performs one specific task, such as calling an LLM, executing Python code, querying a database, or using an external API. After completing its task, 
the node updates the shared state and passes control to the next node.

Simple Definition

A Node is one step that performs one specific job.

Example

Bus booking chatbot:

User Request
      │
      ▼
Understand User  ← Node
      │
      ▼
Search Bus       ← Node
      │
      ▼
Check Seats      ← Node
      │
      ▼
Payment          ← Node
      │
      ▼
Generate Ticket  ← Node

Every box is a Node.

Real-Life Example

Imagine a hospital:

Reception → Node
Doctor → Node
Lab → Node
Pharmacy → Node

====



Each person performs one job.
